        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "EARTH-COVERED ARCH-TYPE MAGAZINES ",
            "block_bbox": [
                344,
                887,
                839,
                908
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "6-37GENERAL ",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                947,
                393,
                970
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Certain types of earth-covered concrete-arch and steel-arch magazines have been approved and standardized for use by the Department of Defense Explosives Safety Board. These magazines provide definite advantages over other types of magazines.Among these advantages are:",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                993,
                1014,
                1096
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1.Less real estate per magazine is required because of the decreased intermagazine separations permitted when approved magazines are used.",
            "block_bbox": [
                205,
                1117,
                1044,
                1168
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2.An almost infinite number of storage situations exists because magazines can be designed to any length.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                204,
                1189,
                1039,
                1238
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3.Because of the reduced separation distances, less roads, fences, utilities,etc., are required.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                204,
                1259,
                1037,
                1308
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Unlike the other structures discussed elsewhere in this manual, an earth-covered magazine is not designed to resist the damaging effects of its exploding contents. lt is accepted that the magazine will be demolished if an internal explosion occurs. During such an incident, the inside of a large-span arch might experience initial blast pressures considerably in excess of 10,000 psi. Less than 100 psi could lift the arch completely ",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                1330,
                1043,
                1463
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "footer",
            "block_content": "6-156",
            "block_bbox": [
                568,
                1485,
                629,
                1505
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": null
        }
    ],
